;##############################################################################
; WAS.EXE - The Ancient Art of War at Sea, CGA version (Broderbund; game (c) 1987 Dave and Barry Murry)
; From the 3.5" disk release (files dated 11 July 1988).
;
; Annotated disassembly, generated by recursive descent from the program entry point,
; the overlay thunk table and every call target, so code and data are separated.
; Every code region is shown at the address it really runs at.
;
; Line format:   region:offset  file-offset  bytes  instruction   ; comment
;   region  rt = resident code (segment 0000), root = startup/loader (segment 06C5),
;           ovl1..ovl7 = overlays (segment 0000, at their load offset), DS = data segment
;   Names in the form ovl3_4a2f / rt_1330 are unnamed functions; named ones are listed below.
;   Names marked "Same code as WAR.EXE" were matched to WAR.EXE.asm by their instruction sequence.
;##############################################################################

;==============================================================================
; MZ HEADER
; file size          162304 bytes
; header             0x400 bytes, 151 relocations
; load image         0x7650 bytes declared (file 0x400-0x7a50)
;                    the overlays and data segment are stored after it, inside WAS.EXE
; entry CS:IP        06C5:02FA  (file 0x734a)
; initial SS:SP      16D8:0100
; linker             Phoenix Software PLINK86 (overlay loader "LINK86 Overlay Loader"),
;                    the same loader as WAR.EXE (1290 of its 1310 bytes are identical)
;==============================================================================

;==============================================================================
; MEMORY MAP (segments relative to the load address)
; 0000:0000-6C4F  rt     resident C code and library: file I/O, text, graphics, sound, game core
; 06C5:0000-051D  root   startup and Phoenix overlay loader (entry 06C5:02FA)
; 0000:72E0        table  overlay descriptor table (16-byte entries, see below)
; 0000:736E-7649  thunks 61 overlay call thunks, called as near calls 0000:736E + 12*n
; 0000:7650-....  ovl1-5 overlay area 1: one of overlays 1-5
; 0000:C9B0-....  ovl6-7 overlay area 2: overlay 6 or 7 (flag 5), resident beside overlay 2, 3 or 5
; 0FF9:0000-3F0F  DS     data segment DGROUP (initialised data, preloaded at startup)
; 0FF9:3F10-....  DS     BSS, buffers, stack (SS=16D8h); DGROUP ends at segment 16E8h
;
; All game code (rt + overlays) runs with CS = load segment, so near calls between them work.
; Data references [xxxx] in this code are offsets in DS (segment 0FF9h).
;==============================================================================

;==============================================================================
; OVERLAY TABLE (file 0x76e0, segment 072E)
; #  file offset  size    loads at       flags  role
; 1  0x07a50     0x59d0  0765-0D02      0000   Main program (as WAR.EXE overlay 1): startup (SCNF, SPM), title and menu screens, scrolls, opponents (SO2, SPJ, AD), Options Shoppe (SPK), battle report (SPN-SPQ), save/load (SS), data disk, the campaign editor flows, hardware detection, key-disk check, campaign loader (S0-SA)
; 2  0x0d420     0x1fb0  0765-0960      0000   Campaign editor: placing ships, fleets and flag ships (SO1); as WAR.EXE overlay 3
; 3  0x0f3d0     0x0fb0  0765-0860      0000   Campaign editor: map maker (SO0); as WAR.EXE overlay 4
; 4  0x10380     0x7a80  0765-0F0D      0000   Campaign play: the sea map, fleets, ports, wind, messages (SO5); as WAR.EXE overlay 6
; 5  0x17e00     0x5360  0765-0C9B      0000   Sea battle (Zoom): ships manoeuvre and fire; calls overlay 6 (and overlay 7 for boarding) through thunks
; 6  0x1d160     0x3370  0C9B-0FD2      0005   Sea battle support, loads at C9B0h beside overlay 5: loads SO6, SO7, SO8; the battle results ("They lost N ships")
; 7  0x204d0     0x35e0  0C9B-0FF9      0005   Boarding: the fight on deck (picture B; Flag, Quarterdeck, Poopdeck, Railing), loads at C9B0h beside overlay 5
; 8  0x23ab0     0x3f10  0FF9-16E8      4000   DGROUP initialised data (flag 4000h = load at startup)
;
; Entry layout (16 bytes, fields shared with the next entry): +4 flags (FFFFh ends the table,
; 4000h preload), +8 load segment, +A end segment, +C file-name pointer (WAS.EXE),
; +E file position in paragraphs; the size in paragraphs is at +2 of the next entry.
;==============================================================================

